=== layout: one-panel
# One Great Idea Form: Product and Science

@body

- Title of your idea: one sentence.
- Brief description: two or three sentences.
- Why you selected the idea: one or two sentences.
- Marketable product: one sentence.
- Living system or biological component used to make it: one sentence.
- Science behind the idea: one or two sentences.
- Steps needed to start producing the product: one or two sentences.

=== layout: one-panel
# One Great Idea Form: Market and Feasibility

@body

- Direct and indirect competitors: "none" is not an acceptable answer.
- Public response and possible controversy: one or two sentences.
- Target customer: individual, government, business, or manufacturer?
- How many products could each customer buy?
- Biotechnology subfield covered in class.
- How much you like the idea.
- How practical and realistic the idea is.

=== layout: one-panel
# Note\: Dr. Voss does NOT choose or reject your idea.

@body

- You are free to choose any topic you like.
- Keep in mind that focusing on a strong biotech topic aligned with the course will make your presentation more persuasive.
- Your goal is to convince your classmates to invest in your idea.
- This assignment is graded solely on completion, not on the choice of your idea.
- There will be NO feedback on the great idea.

